  "description": "of front suspension mountain\nbikes. The Odessa is a dandy little steel bike that softens its ride with\n63mm of RST fork travel. Did I say little? I meant it. Frame sizes go\nall the way down to 13 inches. But they also go all the way up to 22 inches,\nso we can also conclude that the Odessa is big.\n\nThe rear dropouts have eyelets so you can ask your dealer to mount up\na rear rack that can carry a picnic lunch bag, your tennis racket or a\nstack of overdue videos you meant to return on the way back from the coffee\nshop yesterday afternoon. And if you prefer to step through your bike\nrather than swing your leg over the saddle, the Odessa also comes in a\nlady's version. Good for all you kilt wearers, as well.\n\nLooking for a way to add cardiovascular work to your gym workout without\nthe sensory deprivation of riding an indoor bike? Care to wander off the\nbike path once in a while to see where that little path leads? Want to\ntame the bumpy streets of a big, bad city? Or how about slipping into\nwork down back alleys, so far ahead of the gridlock it makes you giddy?\n\nWith an Odessa, all these things are possible.",
